                     <div style="margin-top:8pt;"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">Actual after-tax returns depend on your tax situation and may differ from those </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">shown in the preceding table. </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">When after-tax returns are calculated, it is </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">assumed that the shareholder was in the highest individual federal marginal </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">income tax bracket at the time of each distribution of income or capital gains or
                           </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">upon redemption. State and local income taxes are not reflected in the </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">calculations. </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">Please note that after-tax returns are shown only for the </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">Institutional Shares and may differ for each share class. After-tax returns are </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">not </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">relevant for a shareholder who holds fund shares in a tax-deferred account, </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">such as an individual retirement account or a 401(k) plan. </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:9.5pt;">Also, figures </font></div>
